 "about": "Seeed reBot DevArm at full opening: mujoco_menagerie f3b6013, seeed_rebot_devarm/seeed_rebot_devarm.xml (MIT, Seeed Studio): joint_left/joint_right slide 0..0.05 m on one rack and pinion, q 50 mm (the contact faces 100.15 mm apart).  The bodies are gripper_end's cnc7 (the bracket and the MGN9 rail) and pla7_green (the printed rail supports and end stops), and on each finger cnc_left (the slider extension and the rack); gripper_end's motor_7, the RS-00 actuator, is drawn by the project (below).  The Library mesh is gripper_left's pla_left.STL (the printed finger on its MGN9 carriage) with its contact face's two 1.85 mm pockets capped, in mm.  The other finger is gripper_right: gripper_left turned 180 degrees about the approach axis (0.000 mm, its pla_right.STL and cnc_right.STL), so its sensor is the same board.  The looks: drawn after Seeed Studio's photos of the reBot Arm B601-RS gripper (the Seeed wiki's B601-RS guides: the arm at its zero pose, rs_0pos, and the gripper over a test-tube rack, 00-task-overview-rs-en; 2026-11-17) and its bill of materials (reBot-DevArm's hardware README: the fingers printed in black ABS, the rail supports and end stops in green PLA, the bracket, slider extensions and racks CNC-machined aluminium 5052, anodised or sandblasted, an MGN9 rail): the black printed fingers on their slider blocks, the bead-blasted aluminium of the bracket plate and the slider extensions, the ground steel rail, the lime-green printed supports, and the gripper's RS-00 actuator, a black can.  The actuator is the project's own drawing, not the model's file: plain cylinders and boxes to the sizes of the model's motor_7 (its can 57 mm across and 52 mm long on a 63 mm base ring 15 mm long, its two plug housings), whose 26 480 triangles keep 20 629 within 0.5 mm, 1.03 MB, over the Library's budget for the bodies (bodies/seeed-rebot/drawn-motor-can.stl, drawn-motor-base.stl and drawn-motor-plugs.stl).  The fingers' carriages are the part's own black; the screws and the cables are not drawn.",
